WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.944
Parameters are learned numerical values inside a model.

00:00:04.944 --> 00:00:09.888
Think of many tiny settings that training adjusts gradually.

00:00:09.888 --> 00:00:14.832
A model receives an example and produces an output using its current values.

00:00:14.832 --> 00:00:19.776
The system measures error, then an optimizer changes many parameters slightly.

00:00:19.776 --> 00:00:24.720
During inference, the values stay fixed while they shape results for new inputs.

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:29.664
Parameters shape model behavior; more parameters do not automatically mean better quality.
